Question	Answer
What is page replacement?	Replacing an existing page in memory to accommodate a requested page when no free frame exists.
What is a page fault?	When a requested page is not present in physical memory.
What is a page hit?	When a requested page is already present in physical memory.
What is FIFO?	First In First Out.
What is LRU?	Least Recently Used.
What is Optimal page replacement?	Replacing the page whose next reference is farthest in the future.
Which algorithm produces minimum page faults?	Optimal, for a known reference sequence.
What is Belady's anomaly?	An increase in page faults when the number of frames increases.
Which algorithm can exhibit Belady's anomaly?	FIFO.
Does LRU exhibit Belady's anomaly?	No.
Why is Optimal impractical?	Future page references are generally unknown.
What is thrashing?	Excessive paging that reduces system performance.
What is virtual memory?	A memory management mechanism that provides a virtual address space independent of physical memory capacity.
What is the page fault rate formula?	(Page faults / Total references) × 100.
